SUMMARY:Deadline 23:00 EST: ARCAthens: Athens Residency Fellowships (Spring
  2027)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 14 Nov 2026 at 23:00 EST.\n\nThe Athens Residency is the
  flagship program of ARCAthens\, a not-for-profit founded in 2017\, offeri
 ng fully funded Fellowships for visual artists and curators to live and wo
 rk in Athens. The residency is structured and research-driven\, built arou
 nd arranged studio and private collection visits\, institutional access an
 d community events\, balanced with time for independent work.\n\nOrganisat
 ion: ARCAthens\nLocation: Athens\, Greece (in-person residency). Open to i
 nternational visual artists and curators residing outside Greece.\nAward: 
 Fully funded: housing\, travel\, a Fellowship Prize and a weekly stipend (
 most recent published terms\, Fall 2026: USD 3\,000 Fellowship Prize and U
 SD 200/week stipend\, round-trip airfare reimbursed). No application fee.\
 nDuration: About 12 weeks\, 4 February to 26 April 2027\n\nMore: https://a
 rcathens.org/aa-application/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
URL:https://arcathens.org/aa-application/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Athens\, Greece (in-person residency). Open to international visua
 l artists and curators residing outside Greece.
END:VEVENT
